Verse 1:
[F]Sweet promise [C7]is [F]given to [Bb]all [F]who be[C]lieve—
[F]“Be[C7]hold I come [F]quickly, Mine [C]own [C7]to [F]re[C]ceive;
[C7]Hold [F]fast till [C7]I[F]come; the [Bb]dan[F]ger is [C]great;
[F]Sleep [C7]not as do [Gm]oth[Dm]ers; [Bb]be [C]watchful, [C7]and [F]wait.”
“Hold fast till I come,” sweet [Bb]pro[F]mise of [C7]heaven—
[F]“The [C7]kingdom restored, to you [F]shall [C7]be [F]given.”
[C7]“Come, [F]enter [C]My [F]joy, sit [Bb]down [F]on the [C]throne;
[F]Bright [C7]crowns are in [Gm]wait[Dm]ing; [Bb]hold [C]fast till [C7]I[F]come.”

Refrain:
[F]"Hold [C7]fast till [F]I [Bb]come," sweet [F]promise [C]of heaven--
[F]"The [C7]kingdom [F]restored, [C]to [C7]you [F]shall [C]be given."
[C7]"Come, [F]enter [C7]My [F]joy, sit [Bb]down [F]on [C]the throne;
[F]Bright [C7]crowns [Gm]are [Dm]in waiting; [Bb]hold [C]fast [C7]till [F]I come."

Verse 2:
[F]We'll [C7]"watch [F]unto prayer" [Bb]with [F]lamps [C]burning bright;
[F]He [C7]comes [F]to all [C]others [C7]a "thief [F]in [C]the night."
[C7]We [F]know [C7]He is [F]near, [Bb]but know [F]not [C]the day--
[F]As [C7]spring [Gm]shows [Dm]that [Bb]summer [C]is [C7]not [F]far away.

Verse 3:
[F]Yes! [C7]this is [F]our hope, [Bb]'tis [F]built on [C]His word--
[F]The [C7]glorious [F]appearing [C]of [C7]Jesus, [F]our [C]Lord;
[C7]Of [F]promises [C7]all, [F]it [Bb]stands [F]as [C]the sum:
[F]"Behold [C7]I [Gm]come [Dm]quickly; [Bb]hold [C]fast [C7]till [F]I come."
